The design phase converted the requirements into a clear structure. The system follows a layered architecture in which the camera feeds images to a face detection module, the detected faces pass to a recognition module, the results are stored in a database, and a web dashboard presents the data and generates reports. The application is divided into five modules: registration, face detection and recognition, attendance marking, reporting, and administration with authentication. The database contains tables for students, teachers, classes, and attendance, with the student table holding each person's face encoding. To document the design, a use case diagram, data flow diagrams at level zero and level one, an ER diagram, sequence diagrams for login and attendance marking, and wireframes for the login page, dashboard, and report page were prepared.
